# Shenandoah: traditional American song, printed in Harper's (1882).
{title: Shenandoah}
{composer: Traditional (USA)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}
{x_level: 2}
{x_strum: D - D U - U D U}

{start_of_grid label="Verse"}
| G . C . | G . . . |
| Em . C . | G . . . |
| G . C . | G . Am . |
| D . Em . | C . D . | G . . . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]long to see you,
A[Em]way, you [C]rolling [G]river,
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]long to see [Am]you,
A[D]way, I'm bound a[Em]way, 'cross the [C]wide Mis[D]sour[G]i.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]love your daughter,
A[Em]way, you [C]rolling [G]river,
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]love your [Am]daughter,
A[D]way, I'm bound a[Em]way, 'cross the [C]wide Mis[D]sour[G]i.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
'Tis [G]seven [C]long years since [G]last I saw you,
A[Em]way, you [C]rolling [G]river,
'Tis [G]seven [C]long years since [G]last I saw [Am]you,
A[D]way, I'm bound a[Em]way, 'cross the [C]wide Mis[D]sour[G]i.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I'm [G]bound to leave you,
A[Em]way, you [C]rolling [G]river,
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I'm [G]bound to [Am]leave you,
A[D]way, I'm bound a[Em]way, 'cross the [C]wide Mis[D]sour[G]i.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
